WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
- Four years ago I was
attacked by Beyonce fans

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.903
and this is that story.

00:00:04.903 --> 00:00:05.736
(rhythmic music)

00:00:05.736 --> 00:00:07.720
Before I start this I
want to say something that

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.950
I don't think should matter
in context of this story,

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.040
but it matters to me.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.150
I have been a Beyonce fan

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.910
since Destiny's Child.
(crowd cheering)

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.230
That's before a lot of you were even born.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:21.249
I love Beyonce, but I
wouldn't kill for her.

00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:22.860
(bell tolls)
Anyways.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.460
This all happened four years ago.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:27.540
At the time I was the
animals editor for Buzzfeed.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.090
Basically what that means
is that I was in charge

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:32.210
of all the animals content for the site

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.655
and I would also write posts.

00:00:33.655 --> 00:00:36.040
Buzzfeed pretty much lets
you write whatever you want,

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.490
which is really awesome.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:40.200
So one day, I was finishing up my post,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.340
and I came across this
article that said a panda

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:46.530
had faked her own
pregnancy so she could get

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.110
extra treats and be in air conditioning.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.820
I mean, how amazing is that?

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.160
She saw that other
pandas who were pregnant

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:00.170
got to have special treatment.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.810
That's like the best long
con I have ever heard of.

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:05.220
Honestly, we should just
do an entire video on this.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.460
Anyways, I clearly loved this story

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.530
and I had already hit my quota for the day

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:11.320
so I decided to write
something a little weird.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.990
So the post that I decided
to do about it was writing

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.210
in the voice of a panda saying that it was

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.890
a feminist stance that
she was taking because

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.660
she should be treated well and her worth

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:25.160
shouldn't be based on if
she procreates or not.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.520
I didn't even think that many people were

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.500
gonna see this.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:28.650
I had finished the post,

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.750
I hit publish,

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:30.980
and I went on with my day.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.250
Later that I night, I started getting tons

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.950
of Twitter notifications.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.080
"Bitch, don't fucking hate on the queen.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.690
"Cunt."

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:40.630
"Slut.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.060
"Absolute slut."

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.700
My Twitter handle equals "trash."

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.330
Okay, so this one might be my favorite

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:49.150
"You look like one of
them cheap 65c Barbies

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.010
"at Walmart.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.660
"I hope you catch Ebola
you vanilla chimpmunk

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.350
"built in the face bitch.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:55.400
"Kys."

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.730
What does kys mean?

00:01:58.910 --> 00:01:59.770
- Oh, that's nice.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:02.420
I had never been attacked
by that many people online

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.720
all at once and was
just genuinely confused.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.140
And then I started to notice that a lot

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.660
of the accounts had something in common.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:12.280
They either were Beyonce fan accounts,

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.540
or were hastagging Beygency,

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.730
which only made me more confused.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:20.080
I love Beyonce, and I've never really

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.340
written about her online.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.480
I write about animals.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.400
Did they mistake me for someone else?

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.890
Did they mistake for someone who would

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:27.680
openly shit on a celebrity?

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.300
Did they mistake me for someone
that doesn't like Beyonce?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.930
I did something that you're
never supposed to do.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.360
I fed the trolls.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.300
It wasn't much.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.360
I just replied to one of the tweets

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.770
with a simple question mark,

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:41.690
and all I got back was,
"You know what you did."

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:43.370
But I did not know what I did.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:47.030
Finally, a friendlier
member of the Beygency

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:49.760
tweeted my article about the panda at me.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.730
"Oh, so you happened to use
Beyonce for this article?"

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.310
And then,

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.210
I remembered.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.300
I had used a picture of
Beyonce in my article

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.870
about the panda.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:03.780
She had just done her
amazing MTV performance where

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:07.060
she stood in front of a
sign that said, "Feminist."

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.130
It was nothing short of iconic.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.940
So naturally, when I
was looking for a visual

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:15.100
to describe feminism, I thought of that.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.360
So I slapped a panda
head on Beyonce's body

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.560
and I called it a day.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.210
But realizing this did
not help me figure out

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:22.310
what the problem was.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:26.330
Luckily another nice fan
account tweeted at me,

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.810
"Oh, you don't remember the rumors

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.800
"about Beyonce faking her
own pregnancy two years ago."

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.660
(inhaling)

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:36.180
I was being dragged for
a two-year-old rumor

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.250
about Beyonce.

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.110
A rumor I had completely
forgotten about because

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.650
one, I don't think she
did fake her pregnancy.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:45.700
Two, if she did, none of my business.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.620
Three, there's nothing wrong
with getting a surrogate.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:52.070
Four, why would I use a post about a panda

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:54.930
to really stick it to
Beyonce two years later?

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.350
So I'm in the thick of it,

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:59.160
and I'm trying to explain that
I'm actually a Beyonce fan,

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:01.000
but they just kept piling on.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.640
One person called me a gerbil,

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.500
another called me a pumpkinhead.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:09.350
And one person said Beyonce would end me.

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:12.380
Guys, I don't think Beyonce
cares enough about me

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:15.220
to end me, but I appreciate
that you think she does.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:18.360
So this kind of trolling and mean comments

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.000
and death threats went
on until the morning.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.920
So I get to work and I realize,

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.590
"I think I found my way out.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:26.770
"I have a man on the inside."

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:30.400
So at the time I was sitting
next to internet celebrity,

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:34.410
but more importantly, notable Beyonce fan,

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.410
Matt Bellassai.
(cheerful horns)

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:39.960
So Matt was gracious enough
to pull me out of the rubble

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.360
and tweet at one of the main fan accounts

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:47.290
that I was, indeed, a Beyonce fan.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:50.520
Like magic, it stopped.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.010
The hive had stopped
their swarm for a day.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:56.860
Just a side note, that's
some real power right there.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.650
And with great powers, comes
great responsbeybility.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.480
Can you cut that out?

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.750
So the thing that stuck
with me about all of this

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.570
was that there was so many people willing

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.700
to tell a stranger to
die, or kill themselves,

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.660
over what was ultimately
a misunderstanding.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.280
So I looked at some of
the people's profiles

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.950
because I was curious what
else they tweeted about.

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.340
The rest of their timeline
was just tweeting about

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:21.020
how they were having
a normal, nice evening

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:21.890
with their boyfriend.

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:24.870
And listen, I was, at the time, 26.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.410
Been working on the internet for a while

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.670
and I have a relatively
thick skin about this stuff,

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:29.820
but what if I wasn't?

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:33.720
What if I was 12 or having
an exceptionally bad day?

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.270
I might not be telling this
story as a funny story.

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:39.450
When you're tweeting at
me, like, I'm a person.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:43.540
Overall, I just feel like
everyone needs to chill.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.990
Maybe put on some Beyonce.

00:05:47.473 --> 00:05:50.223
(rhythmic music)

